.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage, editor options, subcommands, and environment overrides.
.TP
.B \-\-help-cmds
List every named editor command and its help text.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the development version and compiled optional modules.
.TP
.B \-\-clean
Load only the compiled panic keymap and retain no workspace state or command
history.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Use
.I PATH
in place of the user
.IR init.fl .
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " NAME"
Override the configured theme for this process.
.TP
.B \-\-no-workspace-config
Do not load the workspace
.IR .yew.fl .
.TP
.B \-\-trust-workspace
Pre-grant the workspace configuration instead of opening the trust prompt.
.TP
.BI \-\-workspace " DIR"
Use
.I DIR
as the workspace rather than the startup working directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-batch " SCRIPT"
Run a Fletch script against the supplied file operands without a tty, grid,
or event loop.
.TP
.BI \-\-replay " REG"
After a successful batch script, replay the one-letter macro register once.
.TP
.B \-\-test
Add the
.B t.*
script-test assertions.
Valid only with
.BR \-\-batch .
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress batch warnings, but not errors.
Valid only with
.BR \-\-batch .
.TP
.BI \-\-grant " NAME:CAP"
Pre-grant a batch plugin one capability from
.BR fs ,
.BR shell ,
.BR net ,
or
.BR clipboard .
Repeatable and valid only with
.BR \-\-batch .
.TP
.B \-\-
In batch mode, pass every remaining argument to the script's
.B args
list.
Outside batch mode it ends editor option parsing.
.SH "E-MODE COMMANDS"
An E command has the form
.BR :[range]name " [arguments]" .
Ranges are one-based lines, marks, searches, or the whole-buffer
.B %
spelling.
The table is generated once from the registry metadata and committed as
literal text; each
.B CMD
row is
.IR "abbreviation | registered command | range policy | argument spec" .
Argument letters are
.B f
for a file,
.B s
for one opaque string,
.B p
for a plugin, and
.B ov
for an option plus value.
.PP
