.PP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
selects configuration;
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
selects plugins and the package lock;
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
selects durable state;
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
selects caches.
Each falls back below
.B HOME
according to the XDG base-directory convention.
.B PATH
locates tools and language servers;
.B PWD
seeds shell-session state;
.B SHELL
selects the command interpreter;
.B TMPDIR
supplies temporary storage;
.B PAGER
is retained only for children that own the real terminal.
.PP
Presence of
.B NO_COLOR
selects monochrome output.
.B TERM
and
.B COLORTERM
participate in terminal capability detection; additional terminal identity
variables such as
.BR TERM_PROGRAM ,
.BR VTE_VERSION ,
and
.B KONSOLE_VERSION
refine it.
.B TMUX
and
.B STY
select OSC 52 wrapping.
.B SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
is consumed by the release build rather than at editor runtime.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Command-line, compilation, ordinary runtime, or explicit refusal error.
.TP
.B 2
A
.B \-\-batch
script failed to compile or ended with an uncaught Fletch error.
.TP
.B 3
File, host, network, or other I/O failure.
.TP
.B 4
An internal invariant failed.
.SH LIMITATIONS
yew preserves file bytes and therefore performs no Unicode normalization;
silently normalizing would rewrite bytes the user did not touch.
Bidirectional layout is not implemented, so right-to-left text renders in
logical order.
Regular expressions omit lookaround and backreferences to retain bounded,
linear-time matching.
.PP
Completion has no snippet-expansion engine.
Panels display plain terminal text rather than rendered Markdown.
There is no interactive terminal buffer; use
.B :!!
to hand the real terminal to a foreground child.
There is no filesystem watcher; explicit refresh and command paths observe
external changes.
Fuzzy matching folds ASCII case only, so non-ASCII names require matching
case.
.PP
In replacements,
.B &
is a literal ampersand; use
.B \e0
for the whole match.
Clipboard register
.B *
aliases
.B +
rather than naming a second system selection.
OSC 52 is write-only; clipboard reads require a readable platform tool or a
configured custom command.
.PP
Plugins are Fletch-only and run without memory or resource isolation.
There is no registry, signing, dependency solver, install hook, or automatic
plugin update.
Git conflict resolution is left to the file editor and external tools rather
than a three-way merge UI.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR yew-fl (1),
.BR yew-pkg (1),
.BR git (1),
.BR less (1)
.SH BUGS
The default log is
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/yew/log
or
.IR $HOME/.local/state/yew/log .
Reproduce a configuration-sensitive problem with
.B yew \-\-clean
and attach the smallest input, terminal name, exact keystrokes, yew version
and module list, relevant log tail, and whether the clean run reproduced it.
